select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'academy', 'chapter', 'hiring', 'Training for every staff function: paths of sections, lessons played and narrated in the browser (no video files are stored), and a quiz per section.

## Progress by staff member

1. Open **People** > **Academy**. Each staff member shows their paths, sections passed and the last quiz. Settings > Staff shows the same count in its Academy column.
2. Open a person: each section with lessons watched, best score, attempts and its state.
3. A section closed for them? Press **Open early**, give the reason and press **Open early** again. The reason is kept.

## Edit lessons and questions

1. Under Paths and sections, open a section. Changes apply at once for everyone.
2. **Edit the title** changes its name and what it covers.
3. Each lesson has **Preview** (the player) and **Edit the lesson**: the title and the scenes. A scene is a caption, the words the voice says, and its picture: a title, a chat between the renter and you, a list, steps, money rows or a rule.
4. **Add a lesson**, **Delete** a lesson; each question has **Edit** (the question, the options, the right answer counted from 0, and why) and **Delete**; **Add a question** at the end.

## The pass mark and the gate

- Settings > Program: Academy: pass mark of a quiz (80% by default).
- Academy gate (on by default): a section opens only once the one before it is passed, and a staff member who has not passed every path of their functions opens only the academy, the guide and their profile. A new hire is held from the start; staff who were already working had a week from release 33 before the hold began. Their progress is kept. Admins are never held. Off: the academy only records progress.
- Release 33 added a section at the end of each path on what changed in releases 28 to 32 (bookings, handovers and returns; licences, photos and agreements; money; cars and listings), with its quiz.
- Take the Admin path yourself from **Take the Admin path**.', 'Academy', 'Training paths by function: progress, opening a section early, editing lessons and questions, the gate.',
  'Training for every staff function: paths of sections, lessons played and narrated in the browser (no video files are stored), and a quiz per section.

## Progress by staff member

1. Open **People** > **Academy**. Each staff member shows their paths, sections passed and the last quiz. Settings > Staff shows the same count in its Academy column.
2. Open a person: each section with lessons watched, best score, attempts and its state.
3. A section closed for them? Press **Open early**, give the reason and press **Open early** again. The reason is kept.

## Edit lessons and questions

1. Under Paths and sections, open a section. Changes apply at once for everyone.
2. **Edit the title** changes its name and what it covers.
3. Each lesson has **Preview** (the player) and **Edit the lesson**: the title and the scenes. A scene is a caption, the words the voice says, and its picture: a title, a chat between the renter and you, a list, steps, money rows or a rule.
4. **Add a lesson**, **Delete** a lesson; each question has **Edit** (the question, the options, the right answer counted from 0, and why) and **Delete**; **Add a question** at the end.

## The pass mark and the gate

- Settings > Program: Academy: pass mark of a quiz (80% by default).
- Academy gate (on by default): a section opens only once the one before it is passed, and a staff member who has not passed every path of their functions opens only the academy, the guide and their profile. A new hire is held from the start; staff who were already working had a week from release 33 before the hold began. Their progress is kept. Admins are never held. Off: the academy only records progress.
- Release 33 added a section at the end of each path on what changed in releases 28 to 32 (bookings, handovers and returns; licences, photos and agreements; money; cars and listings), with its quiz.
- Take the Admin path yourself from **Take the Admin path**.

## The gate, Welcome and waivers (release 34)

- A new hire signs in to **Welcome**: four steps in order (welcome, their profile and phone, the academy, then their first-day tasks). While they are held, Welcome, the academy, the guide and their profile are all they open; any other page brings them back to Welcome.
- Each person''s progress is on their academy page (Admin > Academy, their name) and on their candidate page in Hiring, on the card **Academy gate**: held or open, and the sections passed.
- **Waive the academy** on that card opens their portal at once without the academy. Give the reason: it is kept in the audit log. **Take the waiver back** holds them again until they pass.
- Release 34 added four sections, each with its quiz: pickups and returns (check-in is the pickup, Sign and pay, Book it now, overrides), money (Charge the renter, holds, owner invoices paid outside the platform), listing photos from a shared folder, and the caller panel with renter notes. Staff who had passed everything have a week before the new sections hold them.
- Each section names the guide chapters it was written from. When one of those chapters is published again, the section is listed under **To review: the guide changed** on Admin > Academy: check its lessons and quiz against the guide, then press **Mark reviewed**.
',
  '<p class="gd-p">Training for every staff function: paths of sections, lessons played and narrated in the browser (no video files are stored), and a quiz per section.</p><section class="gd-task" id="academy-progress-by-staff-member" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Progress by staff member</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Academy</b>. Each staff member shows their paths, sections passed and the last quiz. Settings &gt; Staff shows the same count in its Academy column.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open a person: each section with lessons watched, best score, attempts and its state.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A section closed for them? Press <b class="gd-ui">Open early</b>, give the reason and press <b class="gd-ui">Open early</b> again. The reason is kept.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="academy-edit-lessons-and-questions" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Edit lessons and questions</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Under Paths and sections, open a section. Changes apply at once for everyone.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Edit the title</b> changes its name and what it covers.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Each lesson has <b class="gd-ui">Preview</b> (the player) and <b class="gd-ui">Edit the lesson</b>: the title and the scenes. A scene is a caption, the words the voice says, and its picture: a title, a chat between the renter and you, a list, steps, money rows or a rule.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a lesson</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Delete</b> a lesson; each question has <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> (the question, the options, the right answer counted from 0, and why) and <b class="gd-ui">Delete</b>; <b class="gd-ui">Add a question</b> at the end.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="academy-the-pass-mark-and-the-gate" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The pass mark and the gate</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Settings &gt; Program: Academy: pass mark of a quiz (80% by default).</li><li>Academy gate (on by default): a section opens only once the one before it is passed, and a staff member who has not passed every path of their functions opens only the academy, the guide and their profile. A new hire is held from the start; staff who were already working had a week from release 33 before the hold began. Their progress is kept. Admins are never held. Off: the academy only records progress.</li><li>Release 33 added a section at the end of each path on what changed in releases 28 to 32 (bookings, handovers and returns; licences, photos and agreements; money; cars and listings), with its quiz.</li><li>Take the Admin path yourself from <b class="gd-ui">Take the Admin path</b>.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="academy-the-gate-welcome-and-waivers-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The gate, Welcome and waivers (release 34)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A new hire signs in to <b class="gd-ui">Welcome</b>: four steps in order (welcome, their profile and phone, the academy, then their first-day tasks). While they are held, Welcome, the academy, the guide and their profile are all they open; any other page brings them back to Welcome.</li><li>Each person&#39;s progress is on their academy page (Admin &gt; Academy, their name) and on their candidate page in Hiring, on the card <b class="gd-ui">Academy gate</b>: held or open, and the sections passed.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Waive the academy</b> on that card opens their portal at once without the academy. Give the reason: it is kept in the audit log. <b class="gd-ui">Take the waiver back</b> holds them again until they pass.</li><li>Release 34 added four sections, each with its quiz: pickups and returns (check-in is the pickup, Sign and pay, Book it now, overrides), money (Charge the renter, holds, owner invoices paid outside the platform), listing photos from a shared folder, and the caller panel with renter notes. Staff who had passed everything have a week before the new sections hold them.</li><li>Each section names the guide chapters it was written from. When one of those chapters is published again, the section is listed under <b class="gd-ui">To review: the guide changed</b> on Admin &gt; Academy: check its lessons and quiz against the guide, then press <b class="gd-ui">Mark reviewed</b>.</li></ul></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'academy', 'chapter', 'commissions', 'Your training path is under **Me** > **Academy**. There is a path for each of your functions: customer service, fleet, finance, Sales in person or remote, field work.

## Watch the lessons

1. Open **Academy**. Each path lists its sections in order, with Passed, Open or Pass the one before.
2. Open a section. Each lesson is a short video made by your browser: scenes with captions, read aloud by your browser''s own voice.
3. Press **Play**. **Pause**, **Back** and **Next** move through the scenes; **Replay** starts again; Speed goes from 0.75x to 1.5x. **Voice on** turns the voice off and on.
4. No sound or no English voice on your device? The lesson plays with captions only, each scene timed for reading.

> Tip: Use headphones in the office. The voice is your browser''s, so it can sound different on another device.

## Pass the quiz

1. Under the lessons, answer every question and press **Check my answers**.
2. You need 80% (the pass mark in Program settings). Passed: the next section opens. Not yet: each answer shows the right one and why; press **Try again** as often as you need.
3. A section that is on two of your paths (the policies, for example) counts on both once passed.

> Good to know: An Admin can open a section early for you, for example when you already did this work somewhere else. The academy gate is on: each section opens once you pass the one before it, and the rest of the portal waits until you pass your paths (the guide and your profile stay open). Each path ends with a section on what changed recently.', 'Academy', 'Your training path: lessons narrated by your browser, a quiz per section, 80% to pass.',
  'Your training path is under **Me** > **Academy**. There is a path for each of your functions: customer service, fleet, finance, Sales in person or remote, field work.

## Watch the lessons

1. Open **Academy**. Each path lists its sections in order, with Passed, Open or Pass the one before.
2. Open a section. Each lesson is a short video made by your browser: scenes with captions, read aloud by your browser''s own voice.
3. Press **Play**. **Pause**, **Back** and **Next** move through the scenes; **Replay** starts again; Speed goes from 0.75x to 1.5x. **Voice on** turns the voice off and on.
4. No sound or no English voice on your device? The lesson plays with captions only, each scene timed for reading.

> Tip: Use headphones in the office. The voice is your browser''s, so it can sound different on another device.

## Pass the quiz

1. Under the lessons, answer every question and press **Check my answers**.
2. You need 80% (the pass mark in Program settings). Passed: the next section opens. Not yet: each answer shows the right one and why; press **Try again** as often as you need.
3. A section that is on two of your paths (the policies, for example) counts on both once passed.

> Good to know: An Admin can open a section early for you, for example when you already did this work somewhere else. The academy gate is on: each section opens once you pass the one before it, and the rest of the portal waits until you pass your paths (the guide and your profile stay open). Each path ends with a section on what changed recently.

## Your first steps: Welcome (release 34)

Your first sign-in opens **Welcome**, your onboarding checklist, in four steps:

1. Welcome.
2. Your profile and phone: add your home address and your mobile number in your profile.
3. The academy: pass every section of your path. Each quiz passes at 80%, and you can retake it as often as you need.
4. Your first tasks: press **Done** on each one as you finish it.

Until you pass the academy, Welcome, the academy, the guide and your profile are all that opens; any other page brings you back to Welcome. Then **Go to your portal** opens everything.
',
